# Build output, for every crate rather than just the engine's.
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# The terminals.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Journals are trading records — never commit one, not even a test fixture with
# real account ids in it. CI fixtures live in engine/tests/fixtures/ and are
# generated, not recorded.
*.jnl
/data/

# A snapshot is a fold of the journal: balances, owners, open positions. It
# is the same trading record in a different shape, and committing one would
# publish every account in it.
*.snapshot.json

# Where clients are told to send money, and the claims that they have.
# Per-deployment, and a wallet address committed by mistake is one a reader
# might pay to long after it was rotated.
payments.json

# What the house charges on each instrument. Per-deployment pricing, and a
# committed one is a competitor reading your spreads.
markups.json

# The user store holds password hashes. Hashes are not secrets you can use,
# but they are secrets you can attack offline, and a committed one is
# permanent. Every deployment makes its own.
users.json

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Certificates and whatever the proxy caches beside them.
/ops/backups/
caddy-data/
caddy-config/

# Screenshots and references dropped in the working copy while building.
/image*.png
/*.png

.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
